00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.780
in what's today Babylonia, in Iraq, and they were able to study

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.100
their extraordinary advance in astronomy and mathematics.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.780
I'll give you one single example, alright?

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:47.500
With the naked eye, it is impossible to see that there are wounds to Saturn.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.540
Today we know that there are wounds to Saturn because we have a telescope.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:56.060
if you even, you know, just a toy telescope, you focus it into Saturn

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.860
and you could see that there are little moons

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.820
but those things you cannot change with the United Arts

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:10.380
the Babylonians knew, they knew that Saturn had moons, yes

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.900
just to give you another example, you know, there is sunset in the earth

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.140
and there is sunrise in the moon, in the earth

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.640
They know how to calculate the sunset and sunrise in Venus.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:30.000
When the sun rises in Venus and when the sun sets in Venus.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.200
So we're talking about a very advanced culture.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.980
A culture that is, as I say, in many ways, they were going, they were Semitic people.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.980
They spoke a Semitic language, close to Hebrew.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.540
They spoke what we call Aramaic, which is very close to Hebrew.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.000
But they were Gentiles.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:03:05.000
Now in this culture, they had a king, and the king was also God. The king was considered as God, and he was worshipped as God.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:16.000
So you have culture, you have a terrible power in God. You think that Bush is tough? That guy was God. He claims to be God.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:38.000
Yes? That was Nimrod. There was a boy, a little boy, by the name of Avram. Now, there is something about the name Avram. Avram means father, and Ram means haughty. It's the epitome of pride.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:45.000
according to Jewish tradition, Abraham, at the time was not yet Abraham

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Abraham was the greatest scientist of that time, he was the greatest astronomer, the greatest mathematician

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:58.000
and the great man of science, he was the Einstein of ancient Babylonia

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:05.000
alright, now he examined, he studied the universe according to, we don't know what kind of methods he used

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.000
we know that we are very advanced

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.000
and we came to a startling conclusion

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:19.000
that all this universe is the creation of someone

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.000
who is not itself part of the universe

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:28.000
that is omnipotent, powerful, and above is one

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:34.000
and that theory ran against everything that we believe in

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:47.000
Because first and foremost they were apolytheistic. Apolytheistic. They were gods. Those gods were represented by different idols.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:56.000
And not only by different idols, by different clans of priesthood. And I don't mean to pour fun, because that's not the purpose of it.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.200
like today we have, I don't know, Republicans and Democrats and Socialists and Communists and what have you

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:06.480
in those days, you have different kind of priests and every priest has its own god

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:12.240
so all of a sudden you say none of your gods are good, there's only one god

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:22.320
to put it mildly, that is heretical. Now, the story in the Midrashim goes as follows

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:45.340
When Nimrod found out about Abraham Avinu, that he believed in that heresy, namely that there is only one God, you cannot see, you cannot hear, there is no, you cannot represent in an idol, alright? And he created everything and he does everything, which means therefore you Mr. King, you are not really God, you know.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.340
His son is Abraham

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:53.340
and he told him to believe, he says, don't you believe that I am a God?

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:57.340
and Abraham says, yes, you are the God

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.340
let me show you, let me ask you something

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.340
every day the sun rises at the east and sets at the west

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.340
if you are God, why don't you make that tomorrow?

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:11.340
the sun should rise from the west and set at the east

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:31.000
After hearing this, he wrote, he does a famous furnace of fire, he prepares a furnace of fire, he throws Abraham to the furnace of fire. Somehow, a miracle happened. We don't know exactly what happened, but I'll tell you what you will. Abraham immediately said, I know what I'm going to do.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:57.040
There's all kinds of things. According to Haram B'Av, it must have been in the 40s or 50s. Something happened to Abraham afterwards. He leaves Babylonia and he goes to a place called Haram. Haram, I don't know, this is in northern Syria today. Probably by the border with Iraq. I don't know this part.

